1. **Convert the percentage to a decimal:**  
   \( 0.044\% = 0.044 \div 100 = 0.00044 \).  
   This means 0.00044 g of sodium fluoride is present in every mL of solution.

2. **Multiply the decimal by the volume to find the total mass:**  
   \( 0.00044 \, \text{g/mL} \times 10 \, \text{mL} = 0.0044 \, \text{g} \).

3. **Convert grams to milligrams:**  
   \( 0.0044 \, \text{g} \times 1000 \, \text{mg/g} = 4.4 \, \text{mg} \).

The correct answer is \(\boxed{4.4 \, \text{mg}}\).
