5. Gene therapy: This approach involves the administration of drugs or devices that either directly target oncogenic proteins or modulate the expression of genes that control the activity of oncogenic proteins.

By understanding the specific oncogenes involved in a particular cancer, it is possible to develop targeted therapies that specifically target these oncogenic proteins and help to slow or stop tumor growth.
