These regulatory mechanisms help maintain blood pressure within a normal range, despite changes in factors such as posture, exercise, or stress. However, if these regulatory mechanisms are impaired or if the underlying cause of high blood pressure is not addressed, it can lead to serious complications such as hypertension, stroke, or bleeding.
