   - The sympathetic nervous system is activated, leading to an increase in heart rate and force of contraction, which increases blood flow and pressure.
   - The adrenal glands release epinephrine and norepinephrine, which also increase heart rate, force of contraction, and vasoconstriction (shortruption of blood vessels), further increasing blood pressure.
