The treatment for clinical galactosuuria is $\boxed{\text{strict adherence to a galconeamine deficiency diet}}$. This involves severely restricting or eliminating all foods containing glucose, which is a sugar derived from galactose. This deficiency diet ensures that the body does not metabolize galactose, preventing the accumulation of toxic substances and preventing symptoms.

