","The expression of oncogenes contributes to tumor growth by promoting the uncontrolled proliferation of cells, which is a hallmark of cancer. Oncogenes are proteins that promote cell growth and survival, and their excessive activation can lead to the development of cancer. Oncogenes are often encoded by mutated or mutated genes, which can be caused by various factors such as external stimuli (e.g., UV radiation) or internal factors (e.g., mutations during DNA replication).

