The overuse of antibiotics in the treatment of bacterial infections in the general population, in combination with the overuse of antibiotics in the treatment of plant and animal cancers, contributes to the development and spread of antibiotic-resistant bacteria in the environment. This can lead to the development of antibiotic-resistant bacteria in patients, making it more difficult to treat bacterial infections.

