The standard entropies of formation (S°f) at 298 K are:

S°f(CO(g)) = 195.1 J/mol·K
S°f(O2(g)) = 205.0 J/mol·K
S°f(CO2(g)) = 213.7 J/mol·K

Now, we can plug these values into the equation:

ΔS = (3 mol * 213.7 J/mol·K) - (3 mol * 195.1 J/mol·K) - (3.5 mol * 205.0 J/mol·K)

ΔS = 641.1 J/K - 585.3 J/K - 757.5 J/K

ΔS = -601.9 J/K

The change in entropy (ΔS) for the reaction is -601.9 J/K.
