","The key difference between σ (sigma) and π (pi) molecular orbitals lies in the electron density distribution:  
- **σ molecular orbitals** have electron density concentrated along the **nodle** between the nuclei of the bonded atoms.  
- **π molecular orbitals** have electron density concentrated above and below the plane between the nuclei of the bonded atoms.  

In other words, σ orbitals are fully concentrated along the bond axis, while π orbitals are above and below the bond axis.  

\boxed{\text{σ orbital: electron density concentrated along the bond axis (nodle between nuclei)}}  
\boxed{\text{π orbital: electron density concentrated above and below the bond axis (above/below the plane between nuclei)}}
