<start_of_turn>model
","(a) The integral of \( 2^x \) is \( \frac{2^x}{\ln 2} \). Evaluating from \(-1\) to \( 1 \):
\[
\int_{-1}^{1} 2^{x} d x = \frac{2^{1}}{\ln 2} - \frac{2^{-1}}{\ln 2} = \frac{2 - \frac{1}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{\frac{3}{2}}{\ln 2} = \frac{3}{2\ln 2}
\]

(b) The integral of \( 3e^x \) is \( 3e^x \), and the integral of \( 2\sqrt{x} = 2x^{1/2} \) is \( \frac{4}{3}x^{3/2} \). Evaluating from \( 0 \) to \( 1 \):
\[
\int_{0}^{1}\left(3 e^{x}+ 2 \sqrt{x}\right) d x = 3e^{1} - 3e^{0} + \frac{4}{3} \left(1^{3/2}\right) - \frac{4}{3} \left(0^{3/2}\right) = 3e - 3 + \frac{4}{3} = 3e - \frac{5}{3}
\]

(c) The integral of \( 2^{2y} \) is \( \frac{2^{2y}}{2 \ln 2} \). Evaluating from \( 0 \) to \( 1 \):
\[
\int_{0}^{1} 2^{2 y} d y = \frac{2^{2 \cdot 1}}{2 \ln 2} - \frac{2^{2 \cdot 0}}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{4}{2 \ln 2} - \frac{1}{2 \ln 2} = \frac{3}{2 \ln 2}
\]

Final answers:
(a) \( \boxed{\dfrac{3}{2\ln 2}} \)
(b) \( \boxed{3e - \dfrac{5}{3}} \)
(c) \( \boxed{\dfrac{3}{2 \ln 2}} \)
