   \]
   Substituting the volume \(V\) (from the ideal gas law \(pV = nRT\)) yields the entropy in terms of pressure and temperature.

Final answers:
- \(\lambda = \boxed{1.8 \times 10^{-10} \text{ m}}\)
- \(\exp(\mu/kT) = \boxed{10^5 \text{ Pa}}\)
- \(\mu = \boxed{0 \text{ J}}\)
