A diecast component has a mass of 1.2 kg and density 7150 kg/m³ with surface area of 0.075 m². The thermal conductivity of the material is 95 W/mK and the specific heat is 385 J/kg K. It comes out of the machine at 345°C and is exposed to air at 20°C with a convective heat transfer coefficient of 56.8 W/m²K. Determine:  
(i) The temperature of the part after 5 minutes.  
(ii) The time required to reach 50°C.  
(iii) The time constant.  
(iv) The value of convective heat transfer coefficient up to which the lumped parameter model can be used.  
(v) The volumetric area ratio up to which the lumped parameter model can be used.<end_of_turn>
<start_of_turn>model
","(i) **Temperature after 5 minutes**:  
   - The lumped parameter model is valid for this problem because the temperature is uniform within the component.  
   - The temperature of the part after 5 minutes is calculated as follows:  
     \[
     \frac{T - T_{\infty}}{T_0 - T_{\infty}} = e^{-hA t / (m c_p)}
     \]  
     where:  
     - \( T \) = temperature at time \( t \)  
     - \( T_{\infty} = 20^\circ \text{C} \) (ambient temperature)  
     - \( T_0 = 345^\circ \text{C} \) (initial temperature)  
     - \( h = 56.8 \, \text{W/m}^2 \text{K} \) (convective heat transfer coefficient)  
     - \( A = 0.075 \, \text{m}^2 \) (surface area)  
     - \( m = 1.2 \, \text{kg} \) (mass)  
     - \( c_p = 385 \, \text{J/kg K} \) (specific heat)  
     - \( t = 5 \, \text{min} = 300 \, \text{s} \)  

     Substituting the values:  
     \[
     \frac{T - 20}{345 - 20} = e^{-56.8 \times 0.075 \times 300 / (1.2 \times 385)}
     \]  
     Solving for \( T \):  
     \[
     T = 20 + (345 - 20) \times e^{-56.8 \times 0.075 \times 300 / (1.2 \times 385)}
     \]  
     \[
     T = 20 + (325) \times e^{-56.8 \times 0.075 \times 300 / (1.2 \times 385)}
     \]  
     \[
     T = 20 + 325 \times e^{-5.6}
     \]  
     \[
     T = 20 + 325 \times 0.0011
     \]  
     \[
     T = 20 + 0.395 = 20.395^\circ \text{C}
     \]  

(ii) **Time required to reach 50°C**:  
   - The time required to reach 50°C is calculated by rearranging the lumped parameter equation:  
     \[
     t = \frac{m c_p}{h A} \ln \left( \frac{T_0 - T_{\infty}}{T - T_{\infty}} \right)
     \]  
     where \( T = 50^\circ \text{C} \).  
