\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{G b}{d} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{1/2}
\]

Substituting the given values:
- \(G = 26 \times 10^9\) N m\(^{-2}\)
- \(b = 0.286 \times 10^{-9}\) m
- \(d = 6 \times 10^{-8}\) m

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{26 \times 10^9 \times 0.286 \times 10^{-9}}{6 \times 10^{-8}} \left( \frac{1}{2} \right)^{1/2}
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = \frac{7.536 \times 10^3}{6 \times 10^{-8}} \times 0.74
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = 7.536 \times 10^{11} \times 0.74
\]

\[
\sigma_{yr} = 5.54 \times 10^{11} \text{ N m}^{-2}
\]

Thus, the estimated contribution of the hard particles to the tensile yield strength is \(\boxed{5.54 \times 10^9 \text{ N m}^{-2}}\).

