","The entropy production rate \( \Pi_S \) is given by:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{Q}{T}
\]
where \( Q \) is the rate of heat transfer. The heat transfer is due to the work done by the friction force, which is converted into heat. The work done by the friction force is:
\[
dW = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v \cdot dt
\]
where \( dt \) is the time interval. The rate of work is:
\[
\frac{dW}{dt} = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v
\]
This rate of work is equal to the rate of heat transfer, so:
\[
Q = F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v
\]
Substituting this into the entropy production rate equation:
\[
\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}
\]
Thus, the entropy production rate is:
\[
\boxed{\Pi_S = \frac{F_{\text{fr}} \cdot v}{T}}
\]
