   - The piston is in equilibrium, so the net force on it must be zero. The forces acting on the piston are the pressure forces on both sides and the gravitational force.
   - The net force is: \( F = P_A A_A - P_B A_B - mg \), where \( P_A = 500 \text{ kPa} \), \( P_B \) is the pressure in cylinder B, \( m = 25 \text{ kg} \), and \( g = 9.807 \text{ m/s}^2 \).
